      {
        "id": 19715,
        "name": "Tails Adventure",
        "summary": "Tails must stop the Battle Fortress bird army from taking control of Tails Island to rule over the animals.\n\nOn land, in the air, and at sea, Tails battles some pretty tough birds!\nDepending on the Japanese and international version of the game, Tails Adventure is either a prequel or continuation of the Sonic the Hedgehog games for the Sega Genesis. The game mixes traditional platforming and role-playing elements, as Tails is using different items and abilities, as well piloting his creations Remote Robot and Sea Fox, to travel across Cocoa Island to liberate it from the Battle Kukku Empire. Like many Sonic games for the Game Gear, Tails Adventure has been ported onto numerous compilation titles and other games as an unlockable game. It later received a re-release on the Nintendo 3DS in 2013.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co1ztg.jpg",
        "release_date": 811728000,
        "rating": 65.44925318488013,
        "rating_count": 14,
        "genres": "Platform,Puzzle,Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "37,35",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/tails-adventure",
        "cached_at": 1778663167
      },
      {
        "id": 19731,
        "name": "Sonic Labyrinth",
        "summary": "Dr. Robotnik has created a world of 3D mazes, into which he has thrown Sonic and added a whole new dimension to his life! Now the Dude with Attitude can spin dash in every direction - collecting keys to access hidden levels and bonus rooms as he never could before. Can you help guide Sonic through the maze and past the all-new clan of evil Bosses to defeat the damnable Doctor?\n\nIt is also playable on Sonic Adventure DX: Director's Cut and in the PC, Nintendo 3DS, and on the PlayStation 2 and Xbox editions of Sonic Mega Collection Plus. The game features isometric 3D gameplay similar to Sonic 3D. Sonic and Robotnik are the only characters in this game.\n\nSonic Labyrinth was also released on the Nintendo e-Shop for the Nintendo 3DS's Virtual Console on 28 June 2013.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/coar1c.jpg",
        "release_date": 816566400,
        "rating": 56.99286221012078,
        "rating_count": 18,
        "genres": "Platform,Puzzle,Adventure,Arcade",
        "platform_ids": "37,35",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/sonic-labyrinth",
        "cached_at": 1778663167
      },
      {
        "id": 19938,
        "name": "X-Men: Gamesmaster's Legacy",
        "summary": "X-Men: Gamesmaster's Legacy is an action game released in 1995 on the Game Gear. The game starts off with Cyclops and Storm as playable X-Men, although Wolverine, Gambit, Rogue, Bishop, Jean Grey, and Cable can be later unlocked. It is loosely based on the \"Upstarts\" and \"X-Cutioner's Song\" storylines that took place in the comics. It is the sequel to the original X-Men Game Gear game.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co6ivv.jpg",
        "release_date": 792892800,
        "rating": null,
